roman
========================================
roman1.lisp
Simple unordered production system

ROMAN1A is semi-unordered. Validation of input is initial check.
Utilizes PSCOND to display which rules were trigered.
========================================
roman1x.lisp, roman1y.lisp, roman1z.lisp
Similar to roman1.lisp, but these demonstrate that rules can be reordered w/o
consequence. Their rules are literally shuffled from roman1.lisp.
========================================
roman2.lisp
Ordered production system. Conditions of rules are simplified. Consequently, the
order is now significant.
========================================
roman3.lisp
Discrimination net. Rules arranged to minimize number of decisions.
========================================
roman3a.lisp
Better balanced tree than roman3.lisp
========================================
roman-dn.lisp
Discrimination net. Uses DEFNET macro. Supports full range of Roman Numerals up to 3999
========================================
roman-fp.lisp
FP style (Derived from ROMAN1A). No side effects to DB. (Implicit side effect with string output stream.)

ROMAN* is fully side-effect free.
