shrink
========================================
match.lisp
Evolution of the MATCH predicate culminating in MATCH6 (Exported as MATCH).
Tanimoto describes MATCH as being "very much in the production-system style".
It looks like an FP version of PS-MATCH below, using recursive calls rather
than a simple LOOP, and avoiding side effects.
========================================
ps-match.lisp
A more conventional implementation of MATCH as a production system.
This is a hybrid of recursive calls along with destructively modifying the "DB"
as the other production systems do.
